.TH BOSWAS-SYSOPS 8 "November 2026" "boswas-sysops 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-sysops \- the privileged helper of Boswas OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkexec /usr/libexec/boswas/sysops
.I operation
.RI [ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B /usr/libexec/boswas/sysops
performs a fixed set of system operations as root on behalf of the desktop
user: software installation and updates through APT, cleanup, a report of
missing firmware, Flatpak remotes and the Android runtime. Boswas Control
Center and
.B boswas-android
start it through
.BR pkexec (1);
it is never setuid, never a daemon, never runs a shell and never runs an
arbitrary command.
.PP
Each operation has its own polkit action
.BI com.boswas.sysops. operation
(\fI/usr/share/polkit-1/actions/com.boswas.sysops.policy\fR). Read-only
operations are allowed for the active local session; every operation that
changes the system needs an administrator. Remote and inactive sessions are
refused.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B apt-refresh
Refresh the package lists (apt-get update).
.TP
.B apt-upgrade
Install all available updates without removing packages
(apt-get \-\-with\-new\-pkgs upgrade).
.TP
.BI "apt-install " "PACKAGE ..."
Install up to 50 packages from the configured, signature-verified
repositories. Packages excluded by Boswas policy are refused.
.TP
.BI "apt-remove " "PACKAGE ..."
Remove up to 50 packages. Refused when the change would remove a protected
package (Boswas components, essential and required packages, the kernel and
boot chain, the desktop core, the security baseline, APT and dpkg).
.TP
.BI "apt-install-local " /path/to/file.deb
Install a package file the requesting user owns. The file is copied into a
root-only directory before it is inspected. Its origin is not verified by a
signed repository; the device policy can turn this off.
.TP
.B apt-clean
Remove downloaded package files.
.TP
.B journal-vacuum
Reduce the system journal to at most 200 MB.
.TP
.B firmware-report
List firmware files the kernel requested and did not find during this boot,
with the Debian package that provides each one (read-only).
.TP
.BI "flatpak-remote-enable " NAME ", flatpak-remote-disable " NAME
Enable or disable a system-wide Flatpak remote approved by Boswas.
.TP
.BR android-runtime-install ", " "android-runtime-remove " [ \-\-purge\-data ]
Install or remove the Android runtime (Waydroid, from the Waydroid project's
repository with its signing key pinned by fingerprint).
.TP
.BR android-init ", " android-update ", " android-repair
Download and set up, update, or repair the Android system image (without
Google components).
.TP
.BR "android-service start" | stop | restart
Start, stop or restart the Android runtime service (read-only class: allowed
for the active local session).
.SH OUTPUT
JSON Lines on standard output: one
.B start
object, any number of
.B progress
and
.B log
objects, and exactly one
.B result
object, last. Writing
.B cancel
to standard input cancels an operation while nothing has been changed (package
list refresh, downloads); during package installation the request is refused
and the operation completes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
done
.TP
.B 1
failed, or not enough disk space
.TP
.B 2
invalid argument, refused by policy, package not found, or source not verified
.TP
.B 3
another package manager holds the lock
.TP
.B 4
cancelled
.TP
.B 5
a download failed
.TP
.B 6
not supported on this system
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/boswas/apps.conf
Device policy: local packages, Flatpak remotes, Android runtime.
.TP
.I /var/log/boswas/sysops.log
One line per invocation: time, requesting user ID, operation, arguments,
result code.
.TP
.I /usr/share/boswas/sysops/flatpak-remotes/
Flatpak remotes approved by Boswas.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR polkit (8),
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR boswas-control-center (1)
